---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "@/config/site";

const lastUpdated = "1 September 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms & Conditions" description="Terms and conditions for using the JM Travels website and services.">
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container-jm max-w-3xl prose-copy space-y-6 text-body text-charcoal">
      <h1 class="text-display-l text-navy">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <p class="text-body-s text-slate">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        These Terms &amp; Conditions govern your use of the {site.name} website and any travel planning,
        consulting or coordination services you request from us. By using this website or engaging our services,
        you agree to these terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Our role</h2>
      <p>
        JM Travels acts as a travel planning and coordination partner. For many components of a trip (flights,
        accommodation, activities, transfers), we coordinate with third-party suppliers on your behalf. Those
        suppliers' own terms and conditions may also apply to your booking.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Enquiries and proposals</h2>
      <p>
        Submitting an enquiry or form on this website does not constitute a booking. A trip is only confirmed once
        you have received and accepted a written proposal or itinerary and any required payment has been made.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Pricing</h2>
      <p>
        Where prices are shown, they are indicative and subject to confirmation based on availability, travel dates
        and supplier pricing at the time of booking. Final pricing will always be confirmed with you before payment
        is requested.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Visa assistance</h2>
      <p>
        JM Travels does not issue visas and cannot guarantee visa approval. Final decisions are made solely by the
        relevant embassy, consulate, immigration authority or other competent authority. Our role is limited to
        guidance, document preparation support and process navigation.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Cancellations and changes</h2>
      <p>
        Cancellation and change terms depend on the specific suppliers involved in your trip (airlines, hotels,
        activity operators) and will be communicated clearly as part of your proposal or booking confirmation before
        you commit.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        While we take care in selecting and coordinating suppliers, JM Travels is not liable for the acts, errors,
        omissions, delays or cancellations of third-party suppliers, or for circumstances beyond our reasonable
        control (including but not limited to natural events, government action, or carrier changes).
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which JM Travels is registered and operates.</p>

      <h2 class="text-h3 text-navy pt-4">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`} class="link-editorial">{site.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="text-body-s text-slate pt-6 border-t border-mist">
        This document is a general starting point and should be reviewed by a qualified professional for the
        specific jurisdictions in which JM Travels operates before relying on it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
